cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spxa in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "spxa: Stochastic Process Algebra and Computational Graph Engine"
abstract: >-
  spxa is a Python library that treats continuous-time stochastic processes as
  first-class algebraic objects. It provides exact Lévy–Khintchine triplet
  arithmetic with a tracked exactness lattice, a stochastic computational graph
  with reverse-mode differentiation, information geometry, rough path
  signatures, rough volatility, model morphing, stochastic optimal control,
  copulas, and econometric calibration.
